A1. What people treat you reluctantly? ~ SCOTCH
A6. Who goes home cock-eyed every night? ~ TURPIN
A11. What do thoughtful motorists take on a trip? ~ SPARE
A12. What is always singular? ~ ONE
A13. What is a speak-easy? ~ OASIS
A15. What do salesmen do to make their expenses? ~ PAD
A16. What kind of stick do women golfers prefer? ~ LIP
A18. Give the first name of a musical comedy star. ~ ADA
A20. What does a doctor's bill make you? ~ ILL
A21. What are the old family doctors now? ~ SPECIALISTS
A24. What is it to employ? ~ USE
A25. What did Adam do to get his passport? ~ ATE
A27. What adjective means fraudulent, tricky, spurious? ~ SNIDE
A29. Name a pleasant, though shady place. (Plural.) ~ GLENS
A32. Name a famous American row. ~ RUM
A34. What are close relations? ~ KIN
A36. What always gets in the papers? ~ ITEM
A37. What word is often used with the word "again?" ~ NEVER
A38. Who made a beer that even the prohibitionists don't question? ~ HIRE
A39. What is a meadow? ~ LEA
A42. What is good for a drive? ~ TEE
A43. What do borrowers seldom do? ~ REPAY
A46. What made up the passenger list on the Ark? ~ MATES
A49. What is the name of a great old bird of ancient times? ~ ROC
A50. What is an also-ran? ~ NAG
A52. What is the American Blues? ~ PROHIBITION
A57. Name something that has a lot of pull. ~ OAR
A59. Give a masculine nickname. ~ NED
A60. What is a jewel-case for black diamonds? ~ BIN
A61. What does spring inspire in poets? ~ ODE
A63. What should most poetic individuals write? ~ PROSE
A65. Who is the famous old fellow of New Haven, Conn.? ~ ELI
A66. What do people have to do to get into Congress? ~ ENTER
A68. Name a genus of shrubs of the family Rosæoe. (Better try the verticals). ~ SPIREA
A69. What does prohibition do to people? ~ SADDEN

D1. Name a very wet place. ~ SPA
D2. What are vulgar, ill-bred fellows? ~ CADS
D3. What two-letter conjunction is this? ~ OR
D4. What is another name for a sapphire? ~ TELESIA
D5. What are the best steppers of Arizona? ~ HOPI
D6. Name a duck of a bird. ~ TEAL
D7. What is hot stuff to a chicken? ~ ROASTER
D8. Who is a well-known silent pardner? ~ PA
D9. What Goddess taught agriculture and arts to men? ~ ISIS
D10. What means absolutely nothing? ~ NIL
D11. Who keeps watch? ~ SPY
D14. What adjective describes a fox? ~ SLY
D17. What kind of drink is very refreshing? ~ ICED
D19. What magazine would a dumb clockmaker subscribe to? ~ DIAL
D22. What does a humorist thrive on? ~ PUN
D23. What is Big Dick? (Special for crap shooters.) ~ TEN
D26. What is a bird of a note? ~ TRILL
D27. What do daubers do? ~ SMEAR
D28. What is a plaintive, mournful poem? ~ ELEGY
D29. What do silver-lining lookers look for? ~ GLEAM
D30. What are often seen in vaudeville? ~ SKITS
D31. What is a contemptuous look? ~ SNEER
D33. Name a tribe of North American Indians. ~ UTE
D35. What would make Job mad? ~ IRE
D40. What is always parking around? ~ SPOONER
D41. What is a reputation—after discussion in the Sewing Circle? ~ STAINED
D44. What is it always wrong to do? ~ ERR
D45. What is a pain in the neck? ~ ACHE
D47. What is always up against it? ~ ANTI
D48. What is the most noticeable thing about ham actors? ~ EGO
D51. Who has an arresting personality? ~ COP
D52. Name a kind of supporter. ~ PROP
D53. What should be executed as soon as possible? ~ IDEA
D54. What was the sacred bird of Egypt? ~ IBIS
D55. What is the hardest thing to meet? ~ NOTE
D56. What preposition means by; by means of? ~ PER
D58. Give an abbreviation for "a rolling stone." ~ ARS
D62. Where did Daniel put on his act? ~ DEN
D64. What is a Spanish affirmative? ~ SI
D67. Give an abbreviation for a Northern State. ~ ND


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A68: Name a genus of shrubs of the family Rosæoe. (Better try the verticals). → Rosaceæ

